{"title":"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 30","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(credit_to_jeffisepic)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (credit to jeffisepic)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> is equilateral.  Points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are the midpoints of segments <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> respectively.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the point on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a7117fc638a4ea6016e2c316c1ec7dc5bc3176.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2BF=AF$\" width=\"90\" height=\"13\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> denote the intersection of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/5/bc56862b1fdb71204894da278e42ef75de73a40b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/2/c128243ea8125d0bb007b8132dcfa44461df73a7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />,  The value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/2/852b5f62466094b83c986a7304fa71d8e3e9551c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EP/PF$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> can be expressed as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83ce0c4966858ed8ef848e596e2bd7e8f694dc81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m/n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"35\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime positive integers.  Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/d/02dbab3601fa6cce490d54263017048f69e1a35d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"51\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/1/531ea1204366991a65a8c3b8bf1843974a81467a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] import olympiad; size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.7) + fontsize(11pt)); pair A = origin, B = (1,0), C = dir(60), D = (B+C)/2, E = C/2, F = 2*B/3, P = intersectionpoint(A--D,E--F); draw(A--B--C--A--D^^E--F); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,N); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,NE); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,NW); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,F,S); label(&quot;$P$&quot;,P,N); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"225\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/5/6756daa2d442d14b9249c7a3da5b395cfa91e10e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE = EC$\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f35fe2c75c113f7cdd2f6c59a1ca76e728c540b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD = DC$\" width=\"84\" height=\"12\" />, by SAS Similarity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/1/b/21b70807ee89872cbf81b6aa3896691c6e39799e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle EDC \\sim \\triangle ACB$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />.  From the similarity, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/644a8251c0e5e0c6c321e989510fd09d5285f5f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 2 \\cdot ED$\" width=\"104\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36c02644be54c5b6f7b26e07460917fb6c511509.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AF = \\tfrac23 \\cdot AB = \\tfrac43 \\cdot ED$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"181\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/6/89695760c4562a8f31e4f75a3b3344a8da3b92a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{ED}{AF} = \\frac{EP}{PF} = \\frac34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"126\" height=\"38\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd39407010e9423eb7f80f5b26da7f0a240b1858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_2_.28credit_to_jeffisepic.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(credit_to_jeffisepic)\">Solution 2 (credit to jeffisepic)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (credit to jeffisepic)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is the midpoint of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e3a4ec0df571e719bd3f1d7e00bf71fc55ba2b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CB$\" width=\"28\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/d/b1ddd7d108f3d6f0e0e38d5af31b03e762d27efb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD = DB$\" width=\"83\" height=\"12\" />.  By SAS Congruency, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/b/7/eb7f720272a144d27a836616110b98085ca549a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ACD \\cong \\triangle ABD$\" width=\"143\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/6/846c65ce2292a72fa7dd567c88eaa6f049bd37ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CAD = \\angle BAD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"139\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><br />\nBy the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Angle_Bisector_Theorem\" title=\"Angle Bisector Theorem\">Angle Bisector Theorem</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/d/fad662e81d2bf54d7ed0d64709eca1a455b6912a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{AE}{EP} = \\tfrac{AF}{FP}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"71\" height=\"21\" />.  We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/4/854dd0cbf11d42ae026a0421adc2b90ac694f91c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC = AB, AE = \\tfrac12 \\cdot AC, AF = \\tfrac23 \\cdot AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"303\" height=\"21\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f007c491fe5356e3f84da7996f58e38245213704.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac{EP}{FP} = \\tfrac{3}{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"58\" height=\"21\" />.  Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/3/bd39407010e9423eb7f80f5b26da7f0a240b1858.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n = \\boxed{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"94\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_30&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest\" title=\"2006 iTest\">2006 iTest</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems\">(Problems</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Answer_Key&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"2006 iTest Answer Key (page does not exist)\">Answer Key)</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_29\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 29\">Problem 29</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by:<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 31\">Problem 31</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_iTest_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2006 iTest Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> 